
1. pwd — show the current directory
2. ls — list files and folders
3. cd — change directory
4. mkdir — create a directory
5. touch — create an empty file
6. cp — copy files or directories
7. mv — move or rename files
8. rm — remove files or directories
9. cat — display a file’s contents
10. less — read a file one screen at a time
11. head — show the first lines of a file
12. tail — show the last lines of a file
13. grep — search text for a pattern
14. find — locate files and directories
15. chmod — change file permissions
16. whoami — show the current username
17. date — display the date and time
18. df -h — show disk space usage
19. du -sh — show a directory’s size
20. man — open a command’s manual (for example, man ls)
